    <string name="settings_origin">Source</string>
    <string name="settings_origin_text">Logos come preferably via RadioDNS directly from the station (official), otherwise from radio-browser.info. Everything stays stored on this device. RadioDNS on/off under \"RadioDNS\".</string>
    <string name="settings_radiodns_use">Use RadioDNS</string>
    <string name="settings_radiodns_use_hint">Resolves the official logo and matching internet stream from the station identifier (DAB SId / FM PI) at the provider — the same source as the factory radio.</string>
    <string name="settings_radiovis">Live info (RadioVIS)</string>
    <string name="settings_radiovis_hint">Now-playing text and slideshow directly from the station — also for internet streams without embedded track data (e.g. BBC). Needs RadioDNS.</string>
    <string name="settings_slideshow">Show slideshow</string>
    <string name="settings_slideshow_hint">In addition to text, also fetch the station images. Off: text only (saves data).</string>
    <string name="settings_radiodns_refresh">Refresh RadioDNS data</string>
    <string name="settings_radiodns_refresh_hint">Resolve the station-to-broadcaster records again (RadioVIS bearers for live info and the internet fallback) — e.g. if the network was missing the first time or a station was added. Logos come along with it.</string>
    <string name="settings_refresh_button">Refresh</string>
    <string name="settings_auto_fetch_logos">Fetch logos automatically</string>
    <string name="settings_auto_fetch_logos_hint">Automatically fetch missing logos after every DAB scan and at startup. Off: only via the \"Download logos\" button.</string>
    <string name="settings_media_broadcast_logos">Media Broadcast DAB logos</string>
    <string name="settings_media_broadcast_logos_hint">Official DAB logos from the network operator, mapped exactly by SId (best DAB coverage). Downloads ~23 MB on the \"Download logos\" button — turn off when data is limited.</string>
    <string name="settings_ip_fallback">Internet stream as fallback</string>
    <string name="settings_ip_fallback_hint">When both DAB and FM are too weak, keep listening to the station via its internet stream (DAB→FM→internet). Needs a data connection.</string>
    <string name="settings_ip_fallback_wifi">Internet fallback on Wi-Fi only</string>
    <string name="settings_ip_fallback_wifi_hint">Use the internet stream only over Wi-Fi, not over mobile data (data-saving protection).</string>
    <string name="settings_data_usage">Data usage</string>
    <string name="settings_data_usage_text">Logos are fetched once and stay stored. Internet streams only run when the fallback kicks in. When data is limited, turn off RadioDNS or the internet fallback.</string>
    <string name="settings_license_omri">DAB+ reception via hradio/omri-usb (EBU-OMRI implementation). License: GNU LGPL v2.1. Source: github.com/hradio/omri-usb</string>
    <string name="settings_license_radiodns_resolver">RadioDNS resolution via hradio/radiodns (+ minidns). License: GNU LGPL v2.1. Source: github.com/hradio/radiodns</string>
    <string name="settings_license_radiodns">Station logos and internet simulcast are resolved via the open RadioDNS standard and provided by the stations themselves. \"RadioDNS\" and the station brands/logos belong to their respective owners; this app only displays them and is not affiliated with them.</string>
    <string name="settings_license_lgpl_title">LGPL notice</string>
    <string name="settings_license_lgpl_text">The named libraries are under the LGPL v2.1 and can be replaced. The full license text and the source code are available via the projects named above.</string>
